      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(slack): reconcile ambiguous sends before replay",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nSlack can commit a final message while the local sender loses the response. Recovery previously had no exact provider-side proof for that ambiguous outcome, so replay could duplicate the final answer or conservative recovery could strand the queue entry.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n- Attach an opaque authenticated delivery marker to every Slack text chunk. The signature binds the durable queue id, concrete Slack channel, thread target, chunk index, and chunk count.\n- Persist the canonical post-hook reply target and the final pre-API dispatch time in the durable queue, then reconcile only inside a bounded attempt window.\n- Require the complete authenticated chunk set before acknowledging a recovered send. Missing markers remain unresolved because Slack does not expose a supported caller-supplied idempotency key for `chat.postMessage`.\n- Keep exact reconciliation opt-in. Ordinary lower-level required queue sends, media, blocks, and payload transports retain their existing behavior.\n- Try both configured read and write token views when visibility differs, while preserving conflict/incomplete evidence.\n\n## User Impact\n\nAmbiguous Slack final text sends can now be proven from Slack history and acknowledged without posting a duplicate. Thread replies, user-targeted DMs, message chunking, multiple Slack token views, hook-adjusted reply targets, and recovery restarts retain the exact route needed for reconciliation.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Live Slack proof: posted a three-part top-level message and a threaded reply through the rewritten send path; both reconciled the exact authenticated metadata set, dispatch persistence ran once per logical send immediately before posting, and every temporary message was deleted.\n- Slack extension suite: 106 files, 1,459 tests passed.\n- Focused core/Slack regression set: queue storage/recovery, message orchestration, inbound durable delivery, CLI bridge, and Slack adapter/reconciliation tests passed.\n- Testbox-through-Crabbox: `tbx_01kwrgzyhjs49jghs77at7gg96`; `pnpm check:changed` passed core and extension typechecks, exhaustive lint, import-cycle checks, database-first storage guards, and related changed-surface checks. Actions run: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/28732610689\n- Final structured autoreview: clean, no accepted/actionable findings (overall confidence 0.82).\n- No changelog entry: repository policy reserves `CHANGELOG.md` for release generation.\n",
